@@ -70,6 +70,24 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as raw text. Use it when you want text written as-is, without Rich's processing. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("[bold]Hello[/bold]", ":smiley:")
+
+It does the following:
+
+* Writes plain text, with no pretty printing of containers.
+* Does not word wrap or crop the output.
+* Does not interpret console markup or replace emoji codes.
+* Applies highlighting by default. Pass ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's highlight setting.
+* Applies a basic ``style`` if one is given.
+
+Output still goes through the normal print pipeline, so render hooks, capturing, and recording work as they do for print.
+
+
